#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Pi Tin daemon for the Orange Pi Zero 2W (runs as root, pitin-daemon.service).

* Screen brightness: hold SPECIAL and press L2 / R2 (hold to keep changing), or use the web
  page. It sets the kernel backlight (/sys/class/backlight/pitin-backlight, hardware PWM on
  header pin 16), whose scale is already perceptual.
* Volume: SPECIAL + UP / DOWN (hold to keep changing), the same "Master" volume as the web page.
* RGB LEDs, each with its own colour: off, static (steady), wave (a rainbow or the LEDs' own
  colours travel from LED to LED in a chosen order), fade (all LEDs change colour together) and
  reactive (the LEDs next to a button light up when it is pressed). SPECIAL + Y turns them off and on again with
  the same effect, SPECIAL + A changes effect.
* LED auto brightness (led_follow, on by default): the LEDs dim with the screen; their brightness setting is then
  their maximum, at full screen brightness.
* SPECIAL + SELECT pauses the game and shows the list of hotkeys (a RetroArch overlay card); while it is open,
  the buttons do their hotkeys without SPECIAL. The hotkeys show their values as RetroArch's on-screen text.
* SPECIAL + START (quit the game), B (restart it) and L1 (load the saved state) act only when held for a
  second.
* Web page on port 8080 (pitin-web.html): LEDs, uploading and managing ROMs, screen brightness,
  volume, status and power. Optional password: WEB_PASSWORD in /etc/default/pitin.
* Settings are kept in /var/lib/pitin/state.json.
The other hotkeys (save state, slot, menu) are RetroArch's, with its own messages.
"""
